![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

The current sorting logic in `compareRows` sorts by multiple fields using arithmetic subtraction, which can yield NaN and cause unstable sorting. We should simplify `compareRows` to sort lexicographically by the ID field (`question_key`) using a null-safe natural string comparison to prevent diff churn and maintain consistency.

```javascript
function compareRows(left, right) {
  const leftId = normalizedString(left.question_key);
  const rightId = normalizedString(right.question_key);
  if (leftId < rightId) return -1;
  if (leftId > rightId) return 1;
  return 0;
}
```

<details>
<summary>References</summary>

1. When sorting alphanumeric or potentially non-numeric identifiers, avoid arithmetic subtraction. Use a null-safe natural string comparison instead.
</details>

